 "correction_note": "Prior reading compared c_split against the placebo c_noise_placebo. That is wrong: c_split is estimated from two independent trace halves (no shared measurement error between regressor and outcome), so it is ALREADY the decorrelated estimate and should be compared to 0 directly. The placebo instead explains c_original's bias: c_original = c_true + bias, c_noise_placebo ~= bias under the shared linear-measurement-error model, so c_original - c_noise_placebo should approximate c_split. Verified below (c_original_minus_c_noise vs c_split, 'agrees_within_tolerance' at +/-0.03) for every step -- holds everywhere, exactly (S6: both give -0.039) to within the tolerance (S1: 0.030).",
